aking them thinner lighter and more  powerful  even adding a thunderbolt 3 port on the  2016  dell xps but then apple did something  that shocked the world  they completely scrapped all of their  ports on the 2016 macbook pro  and went with a simple set of four  thunderbolt 3 ports  which sparked the rise of usbc which  eventually went mainstream  and if you haven't seen my video on  apple's usbc  master plan definitely check it out  because it's very eye-opening  but going back to the dell xps in 2018  they completely ditched the usb-a ports  and went with  thunderbolt 3 ports while at least still  keeping an sd card slot  now at this point something very  interesting began to happen  premium windows laptops started to catch  up to apple's macbooks in terms of the  pricing  especially with the 2019 dell xps which  got an  even more premium chassis and just last  year  we compared the latest dell xps 13 to  apple's  10th gen intel macbook pro and the  results were  very interesting a similarly spec'd xps  13 model  was only a hundred dollars cheaper than  the 1800  macbook pro and the xps had many  shortcomings  like having a much worse trackpad having  inferior speakers  a worse webcam much worse microphones  and only half the thunderbolt 3 ports so  at that point  apple's macbook pros didn't seem like  that bad of a deal after all  since many premium laptops with matching  specs  were already getting close to the same  price of the macbook pro  so the overpriced macbook narrative  started to die down a little bit  the only real issue that remained was  that apple's intel  macbook air was hugely flawed with  overheating  issues that caused the fans to spin up  really loud  and the performance was pretty terrible  forcing us to recommend apple's  1800 macbook pro if you really wanted a  great macbook  but then in november of 2020  everything changed apple revealed the  brand new m1 chip  that went into the macbook air the  macbook pro and  the mac mini this chip basically blew  everyone's minds including ours  especially since it allowed the  passively cooled macbook air  to obliterate the previous intel-based  air  almost matching up to the performance of  the m1  macbook pro for 300 more and not only  did it have  excellent performance but it came with  killer battery life compared to windows  laptops and it was priced at only 999  dollars  with it being on sale right now on  amazon for only 8.99  so for the first time ever we decided to  compare the m1 macbook air  to a fully loaded 16 inch macbook pro  for 38.99 and to our surprise  the m1 air outperformed it in terms of  multi-core performance  it almost matched up in terms of logic  pro music production  it actually destroyed the 16-inch for  xcode programming  it almost matched up for lightroom photo  editing  and it actually matched up or even  exceeded it  for some video editing tasks like atvc  stabilization and 10 bit 422  rendering this basically blew our minds  and at this point it was clear that  windows laptops were in  deep trouble at this point apple's 1300  m1 macbook pro was greatly outperforming  dell's even more expensive xps 13  options  while also getting much better battery  life  we also tested razer's brand new razer  book 13  which was actually more expensive at  sixteen hundred dollars  compared to a similarly spec fifteen  hundred dollar m1 macbook pro  and the m1 smoked it across the board  and then we compared the m1 macbook air  to microsoft's brand new surface laptop  4s  both the intel and amd models and the m1  basically destroyed them being a much  better value for the price  but the nail in the coffin was us  comparing the 999  m1 macbook air to lg's brand new  gram 14 laptop for 11.99  and the m1 was better in basically  everything  from performance to build quality and at  that point  i realized that apple had succeeded with  the first  phase of juking the windows laptop  market  by getting them to follow in their  footsteps by improving their materials  which led to laptop prices almost as  high as apple's macbooks  and out of nowhere apple swooped in with  the m1 chip  causing their lower end macbooks  especially the m1 macbook air  to outperform out value and  outlast the batteries of the windows  laptop competitors  all at the same time this is a massive  issue for the windows brands out there  because they don't currently have access  to high-end arm chips like apple does  so if they want to stay competitive they  need to lower the prices of their  laptops  and because apple juked them into using  higher and higher quality materials and  parts  they're kind of stuck in a box because  they're either going to have to accept  lower profit margins if they lower their  prices  or they're going to have to lower the  quality or the specs of their laptops  compared to their current models which  is going gonna cause  outrage within the laptop community and  that's probably why we've recently been  seeing many lifelong windows users  finally decide to switch over to the mac  all because  of the groundbreaking m1 chip and with  each day that  passes more and more software companies  are continuing to optimize their apps  for apple silicon like adobe which just  announced  native m1 apple silicon support for  premiere pro  media encoder and character animator and  get this  the m1 macbook pro is now twice as fast  as a windows  desktop pc with the best of the best rtx  3090 gpu in terms of scene edit  detection in premiere pro  but all of that was just the first phase  of apple  juking the laptop market so now let's  get into the second  future phase apple's m1x macbook pros  are getting released within the next  couple of months  and they're literally going to shock and  revolutionize  laptops forever unlike with the m1 max  apple is now going to be focusing on  maximizing performance  with the m1x chip and based on reports  from mark german  the most reliable apple leaker out there  the chip will come with 8  high performance cpu cores 2 efficiency  cores  and either 16 or 32 graphics cores  and based on my calculations it will  outperform  every laptop chip ever made in terms of  cpu performance  with a geekbench multi-core score of  over 14  000. on top of that we're expecting the  32 core gpu model  to score around 80 to 90 000 points in  the metal graphics test  performing around as well as an rtx 3060  gaming laptop  but keep in mind that the gpu in the m1x  is going to be fully  integrated into the soc package  providing extra benefits  due to the unified architecture but on  top of all of that  the m1x macbook pro is gonna once again  juke the premium windows laptop market  by bringing everyone's favorite ports  back  based on reliable reports from mark  german as well as leaked apple  schematics  apple is bringing back the sd card slot  the hdmi port  and the magsafe charging connector on  the m1x macbook pros  and meanwhile dell's brand new xps 13  is still stuck with two thunderbolt  ports and a micro sd card slot  so it's pretty obvious that they'll be  following in apple's footsteps again  to bring back some of those ports and  once these m1x macbook  pros are on the market they're gonna  shake up the entire industry  and cause windows laptop brands like  dell to scramble  trying to get their hands on arm-based  chips to throw into their laptops  so they can compete in terms of  performance and battery life  and that right there is gonna be the  laptop revolution  that apple masterminded now if you  totally disagree with my thoughts  then go ahead and comment your thoughts  down below but if you enjoyed the video  definitely click the circle above to  subscribe and check out one of those two  videos  right over there thanks for watching and  we'll see you in the next video

